hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15658","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu Bishr informed us, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man comes to me asking me a sale not with me what I would sell to him, then I sell to him from the market. So he said: Do not sell what is not with you."
"15659","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, that he heard Urwah and Said ibn al-Musayyab saying: We heard Hakim ibn Hizam saying: I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then he said: Indeed this wealth is green sweet. Whoever takes it with its right, it is blessed for him in it, and whoever takes it with craving of soul, it is not blessed for him in it, and he is like one who eats and is not satisfied. The upper hand is better than the lower hand."
"15660","It was recited to Sufyan: I heard Hisham, from his father, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I freed in the pre-Islamic period forty freed slaves. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have embraced Islam upon what preceded for you of good."
"15661","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Khalil, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Hashimi, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The two sellers have the choice so long as they have not separated. If they are truthful and explain, they are given blessing in their sale, and if they lie and conceal, the blessing of their sale is wiped."
"15662","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: I heard Musa ibn Talhah, that Hakim ibn Hizam narrated to him, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best charity, or the most excellent charity, is what leaves sufficiency, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."
"15663","He said: Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah informed us, from his father, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and let one of you begin with those he supports, and the best charity is what is from surplus sufficiency, and whoever seeks sufficiency Allah will suffice him, and whoever seeks chastity Allah will make him chaste. So I said: And from you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And from me. Hakim said: I said: My hand will never be under the hand of a man among the Arabs ever."
"15664","Waki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shuaythi narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Madani, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Prescribed punishments are not carried out in mosques, nor is retaliation taken in them."
"15665","Hajjaj narrated to us, al-Shuaythi narrated to us, from Zufar ibn Wathimah, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: Mosques, poems are not recited in them, and prescribed punishments are not carried out in them, and retaliation is not taken in them. My father said: He did not raise it, meaning Hajjaj."
